Captured continuations can now be called like functions on all four VMs. The full JVM and CLJS test lanes pass. cljstyle did not run because the harness needed an approval I didn't get. Nothing is staged or committed, and the full report is at `collab/1790766815406-vm-engineer-continuation-invocation.claude-opus-5-5.report.md`.

Calling a continuation with one argument drops the current continuation and delivers that argument to the capture point. The store is not rolled back, and a continuation can be called more than once, including after the expression that captured it has returned. Any other number of arguments throws `"Continuation expects exactly one argument"`, with the same message on every VM. No AST tags or grammar changed, and nothing under `yin.repl`, `dao.jing` or `dao.stream` was touched, so it doesn't conflict with the DHT work.

**What changed:**
- **`engine.cljc`:** two shared helpers, `reified-continuation?` and `continuation-argument` (which checks arity and throws the shared message).
- **`ast_walker.cljc`:** one new case in `apply-function`.
- **`semantic.cljc`:** one new case in `apply-call` that jumps back to the captured position and state.
- **`debruijn/stack.cljc`:** one new case in `:call` that reuses the existing `stack-restore`.
- **`debruijn/register.cljc`:** `register-restore` is split into two helpers, `check-format!` and `write-back`, without changing its behaviour. `:call` now uses them to invoke a continuation.
- **Tests:** a new `test/yin/vm/continuation_invoke_test.cljc` runs five tests on every VM: escape (result 9), tail-position call (8), re-entry after return with a store counter (`[30 3]`), store not rolled back (`[1 :written]`), and the 0- and 2-argument errors.
- **Docs:** `ast.md` and `co-routines.md` are updated, replacing the "Currently ... throws" text.

